{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfe2CDYFDTLyQ8DnNGmxR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've submitted the portfolio. It scored a training Sharpe of 2.47 and a validation Sharpe of 0.47 (2000–2012).\n\nI chose not to search over the validation set. You allowed up to 5,000 backtests, and tuning against them would almost certainly have pushed the validation number higher. But that number would then be a selection result, not an honest out-of-sample estimate. So I built and chose the method using only the 1970–1999 training data, and called the validation backtest once, on the final portfolio.\n\n- **Signals are mostly noise:** single-signal training Sharpes cluster near zero. They spread out by about 0.2, which is roughly what 30 years of noise alone would produce.\n- **Gains don't carry over:** to compare methods, I split the training period and tested each method on the part it wasn't fitted to. Sharpe dropped from about 2.5–4.5 within the fitting period to at most about 0.7 on 1990s data, and to about −0.1 to −0.2 on 1970s data. Optimisers fitting harder on the training data, like mean-variance, did worse out of sample. The simple weighting below was about as good as anything else.\n- **The 0.47 validation Sharpe** is in line with that out-of-sample range. The gap from training (2.47) is mostly overfitting to the training period.\n\nPortfolio description: Every one of the 423 signals is held with weight equal to its 1970–1999 Sharpe ratio divided by its volatility, so each signal is traded in the direction its training performance suggests and sized by risk. This diversified, lightly fitted portfolio was chosen over more aggressive optimisers because it held up best on held-out parts of the training data, and it scored a single validation Sharpe of 0.47."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":491,"cache_read_input_tokens":9783,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":491},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f06cb5c6-7440-4705-8d5d-c192386040f5","uuid":"2079b35d-5d4e-42c1-b91c-261ab14f07c4","timestamp":"2026-10-02T20:13:11.933Z","request_id":"req_011Cfe2CDJrzz9nJwF4hGwMd"}
